 import numpy as np
 
+# Largest emptying number dt_s * (sum of a donor patch's edge coefficients) the implicit runoff step uses (post-
+# reconstruction addition of 2026-10-07). On the thick branch the shear-driven flux V_s delta_m / 2 does not vanish
+# with the film, so the emptying rate q / (A b) of a nearly dry patch grows like 1/b: on the 100 mm default flight
+# (seeds 12345 and 2, ~110 s) a patch holding 5e-39 kg reached dt_s * out = 5e34, the 1 of the diagonal 1 + dt_s * out
+# was lost to round-off, the columns of two such patches summed to exactly zero and SuperLU found the matrix exactly
+# singular. A donor whose emptying number exceeds EMPTYING_MAX keeps a fraction 1 / (1 + dt_s out) < 1e-12 of its film
+# over the sub-step either way, so its coefficients are scaled down to this bound: the solve stays an M-matrix whose
+# diagonal dominance is representable (to ~1e-4 of the 1), the transport stays conservative, and nothing changes
+# unless a patch exceeds the bound.
+EMPTYING_MAX = 1.0e12
 
